# Cursor AI Rules for DrillDraw Project

## Critical Rules

- **Never work on main branch.** Always create a branch with an issue number first.
- **Pre-work:** Check branch (`git branch --show-current`). If on main, create branch `type/issue-number-description`, then start work.
- **Pre-commit:** Run `flutter analyze`, `dart format .`, `flutter test`, then commit. Fix all issues before committing.

## Documentation Map

Use these files for detailed rules. Cursor should read them when relevant:

- **Workflow** (branch naming, git, commands, troubleshooting): `.cursor/rules/workflow.md`
- **Architecture**: `.cursor/rules/architecture.md`
- **PR and planning**: `.cursor/rules/pr-flow.md`
- **Testing**: `.cursor/rules/testing.md`
- **Code quality, performance, canvas, review**: `.cursor/rules/code-quality.md`
- **Glossary**: `.cursor/rules/glossary.md`
- **ADRs**: `docs/ADR-*.md`

## Memory Reminders

- Never work on main branch.
- Always create branch with issue number before starting work.
- Always run `flutter analyze` before committing.
- Always run `dart format .` before committing.
- Always run `flutter test` before committing.
- This applies to all work, including documentation.
